<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<package xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/packaging/2012/06/nuspec.xsd">
    <metadata>
        <id>GX.Blazor.Template</id>
        <version>1.7.1</version>
        <title>GX Blazor Server Solution Template</title>
        <authors>GX Informatics Limited</authors>
        <description>
            A Blazor Server solution template for .NET 10, laid out in Clean Architecture layers.
            Ships ASP.NET Core Identity with permission claims over a multi-tenant DATA MODEL,
            deny-by-default authorization on every request, transactional audit trails, structured
            logging into a separate log database, and Documents and PicklistSets as worked examples.
            Tenant isolation is enforced for Documents, the Users area, audit trails, online presence
            and picklists - the first three with a named cross-tenant right, presence and picklists
            deliberately with none; system logs remain installation-wide. Roles stay installation-wide
            by design, but DEFINING one needs a named, revocable right. Picklists are shared reference
            data plus per-tenant additions, and creating a shared value needs a named right too. See
            the Tenancy section of the README before relying on it.
        </description>
        <summary>
            Blazor Server solution template for .NET 10 in Clean Architecture layers, with a
            multi-tenant data model, deny-by-default authorization and transactional auditing.
        </summary>
        <releaseNotes>
            1.7.1
            - Module services: a ModuleServices&lt;TModule&gt; per module per layer (and one AppLevelServices for code
              that belongs to no module) registers the module's services, seeders and Contracts implementations,
              found by scan; no module edits a DependencyInjection file. Order: template, then modules by
              ModuleDefinition.Order and name, then the application level. Startup fails for a silent replacement
              of a registered service (use Replace&lt;,&gt;, which is logged), an EF interceptor, or a Contracts
              interface not registered exactly once ([NotAService("reason")] exempts a shape or marker).
            - Permissions decided by attribute: [AdministratorGrant] / [AdministratorExcluded("reason")] decide any
              constant outside the template's lists, in a module or the application level.
            - Role catalogue: AddApplicationRole / GrantToRole, reconciled at every start (grant, never revoke).
              The administrator role is never named. An administrator holding an approval permission is logged
              at Error on every start; the approval is refused when sent.
            - Branches: AddEditBranchCommand runs in a unit of work and raises BranchCreated, BranchChanged and
              BranchDeactivating, which handlers may veto; the saved branch is granted to the command and its
              handlers (IBranchDefiningCommand). Module validators show on the dialog's fields.
              BranchScreenOptions replaces the dialog and the page (the template page redirects).
            - A user with assigned branches has exactly one default (refused otherwise; PostgreSQL partial unique
              index; existing users repaired at startup).
            - Application-level code (AppLevel folders): may send module commands and use Contracts; no module may
              reference it; it holds no entities.
            - The template's tests assert the template's own parts, not "nothing else exists", so a generated
              project with modules stays green; every release's smoke test now proves it with a sample module.

            1.7.0
            - Approvals: IApprovable&lt;T&gt; documents are approved only by an IApprovalCommand&lt;T&gt;, which
              ApprovalBehaviour checks inside the unit of work, with the header locked. Nobody approves what they
              prepared or created. The administrator and background work never approve. The approver's limit
              (ApprovalLimits, by role and document type, optionally per branch) must cover the stored value.
              Branch scope is optional. [ApprovalPermission] constants may never be granted to the administrator,
              and the UI refuses to give them to an administrator. A save that approves outside an approval
              command fails. Approval Limits page under System > Authorization.
            - Modules and schemas: [Module&lt;TModule&gt;] puts an entity's table in its module's schema (core is
              retired). Startup fails for an application entity with no module, a navigation across modules,
              or two tables with one name. Configurations under Infrastructure/Modules are applied. Modules
              add menu sections through IMenuContributor and reach their entities through Set&lt;T&gt;(), not
              DbSet properties.
            - Architecture tests in every generated project:
              - module boundaries, read from IL, including lambdas, async methods, iterators, local functions,
                Razor components and generic arguments;
              - no cross-module navigation;
              - no cacheable query of ledger or branch-scoped tables (refused at run time);
              - only AcrossBranchesAsync removes the branch filter;
              - raw SQL only in listed files;
              - idempotent requests return Result, checked at startup;
              - no DbSet of a module entity.
            - IInsertIfAbsent: a concurrency-safe INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING for rows a posting creates,
              honouring the branch grant, decimal kinds and audit fields.
            - Errors: no exception text reaches a user (the unused exception handlers were removed; mail and
              storage return a reference); PostingRejectedException keeps its message outside a unit of work;
              Result.ErrorCode carries a machine-readable code.
            - A user deactivated, or locked out by an administrator, while signed in is refused on their next
              action and signed out. A lockout from failed sign-ins only blocks new sign-ins.

            1.6.0
            - Money and quantities: every decimal declares [Money], [Quantity], [UnitCost] or [Rate], which sets
              its precision; startup fails for an undeclared decimal or an unmarked float/double, and a value with
              more decimal places than its kind is refused at save. GxRound rounds midpoints away from zero.
            - Concurrency: IVersioned / BaseVersionedEntity map Version to PostgreSQL xmin. Edits carry the loaded
              version (IVersionedEdit, ApplyLoadedVersion) and saves return the new one (Saved&lt;TId&gt;); a stale
              edit gets "This record was changed by someone else". PicklistSet and Branch are versioned.
            - Posted records: IAppendOnly ledger rows are never updated or deleted (with database triggers via
              CreateAppendOnlyTrigger); IPostable documents and their IPostableLine lines change only in
              [AllowedAfterPosting] properties once posted; bulk writes to these tables are refused.
            - Users are deactivated, never deleted; Permissions.Users.Delete is retired.
            - Branches: Branch and UserBranch, a branch query filter on IMustHaveBranch and IBranchVisibility
              entities, IBranchCommand checked fresh on every send (Branches.WriteAll for head office),
              AcrossBranchesAsync for permitted cross-branch reads, a Branches page, user-dialog assignments
              and a top-bar active-branch switcher.

            1.5.0
            - Posting transactions: a request marked ITransactionalRequest runs in one context, connection and
              transaction with the PostingEvents it raises (IPostingEventHandler), which commit or roll back
              with it; ordinary domain events are published only after the commit. Nested transactional
              requests join the outer one. Deadlocks and serialisation failures retry the whole request.
            - PostingRejectedException carries a business rejection to the user; other exceptions now show a
              fixed message with a reference id, and database update failures are logged.
            - Idempotent requests (IIdempotentRequest), gap-free document numbers (IDocumentNumberAllocator)
              and row locks (ForUpdate), PostgreSQL only. New tables ProcessedRequests and DocumentSequences.
            - Cache invalidation runs after the commit; cacheable queries bypass the cache inside a transaction.
            - Profile photos and document images are processed with SkiaSharp instead of ImageSharp (pass 47b).

            1.4.0
            - Apps carry their own ICU (Microsoft.ICU.ICU4C.Runtime, System.Globalization.AppLocalIcu),
              so IANA time zone ids such as Africa/Lagos resolve on Windows Server 2019 and older; the
              startup log says which ICU is in force.

            1.3.0
            - Tenancy by marker: every IMustHaveTenant / IMayHaveTenant entity is tenant-filtered and
              stamped from its marker, and startup fails if a marked entity ends up unfiltered.
              Documents are now filtered too: a principal with no tenant sees only tenantless ones.
              ITenantSeeder seeds each tenant on creation and reconciles every tenant on start;
              ISystemContext runs background work as the gx-system account inside one tenant.
              TenantUsers gets a unique (TenantId, UserId) index; tenant Create and Update are
              separate commands with separate rights.
            - BaseEntity&lt;TKey&gt; and BaseAuditableEntity&lt;TKey&gt;: any key type, with domain events and
              audit stamping kept. IApplicationDbContext.Database lets a handler own a transaction.
              The startup authorization check covers commands and queries and refuses struct
              requests. Table naming handles TPT, TPC, many-to-many joins and [Table].
            - The package carries no editor or agent state (.claude, .vscode, .idea, .cursor), and
              records the git commit it was packed from in its repository element.

            1.2.0
            - The theme drawer is gone. One light/dark toggle sits in the app bar; with no saved choice
              the device's preference decides, and no page paints in the wrong theme first. The drawer's
              colour picker, right-to-left toggle and online-users roster went with it.
            - GxSubmitButton: every button that submits or does work shows its progress (spinner, busy
              label, aria-busy) and cannot run twice; never the disabled attribute. gx-busy-button.js
              covers real form posts. MudLoadingButton and the hand-made busy flags are removed, and
              SubmitButtonGuardTests keeps a plain submit MudButton out.
            - Dialog actions run inside their dialog: user and role deletes, clearing the logs and
              resetting a password show progress there, and a refusal stays in the dialog instead of a
              snackbar after it closed.

            1.1.0
            - Nothing calls out by default. Removed: the unused MaxMind GeoIP web-service client, the
              Google Fonts link, the qrcodejs CDN script loaded on every page, and the unreferenced
              components and scripts that loaded Swiper, Fancybox, fabric.js and a second copy of
              OpenSeadragon from CDNs. The document image viewer still loads OpenSeadragon from unpkg.
              The upstream Seq sink and seeded Gravatar pictures were already removed.
            - OutboundAddressTests: a hard-coded http(s) address in src/ fails the tests unless it is
              on the test's allowed list with its reason.
            - Every pass since 1.0.0 (test infrastructure on PostgreSQL, configuration layout, mail
              over the Mailgun API); see the repository's pass reports.

            1.0.0
            - First GX release, derived from CleanArchitectureWithBlazorServer.
            - Deny-by-default request authorization with a startup assertion.
            - Audit rows written in the same transaction as the change they describe.
            - Structural per-principal cache scoping.
            - Demo features (Products, Contacts, chatbot, document OCR) removed.
        </releaseNotes>

        <license type="expression">MIT</license>
        <requireLicenseAcceptance>false</requireLicenseAcceptance>
        <copyright>Copyright (c) 2019 Jason Taylor and contributors; portions copyright (c) GX Informatics Limited</copyright>
        <tags>blazor blazor-server clean-architecture multi-tenant dotnet10 template csharp</tags>
        <icon>icon.png</icon>
        <readme>README.md</readme>

        <!--
            The commit this package was packed from, so an installed template can always be traced
            back to its source. $commit$ is filled at pack time by build/pack.csproj from
            `git rev-parse HEAD`; packing fails if it cannot be resolved, and the pack assertion reads
            it back out of the produced package.
        -->
        <repository type="git" url="https://github.com/GXInformatics/GXTemplate.git" commit="$commit$" />

        <packageTypes>
            <packageType name="Template"/>
        </packageTypes>
    </metadata>

    <files>
        <!-- The package icon and readme, at the package root, which is where the <icon> and
             <readme> elements above look. -->
        <file src=".template.config\icon.png" target="icon.png"/>
        <file src="README.md" target="README.md"/>

        <!--
            Everything the template instantiates, under content/.

            .template.config MUST be included: template.json and ide.host.json are what make this a
            template package rather than an ordinary one, and excluding them produces a package that
            installs without error and offers no templates.

            LICENSE and README.md are included too - a generated project should carry its licence and
            its documentation.

            EVERY exclude pattern below must begin with **\. NuGet matches these against the
            resolved absolute path of each file, so a root-anchored pattern such as docs\** is
            compared against C:\...\GXTemplate\docs\... and never matches - it excludes nothing,
            silently. That is not hypothetical: docs\** and doc\** matched nothing and shipped
            6.5 MB of screenshots and design notes inside the package until Pass 9.

            **\src\Server.UI\appsettings.Development.json is the maintainer's OWN local file, with
            their local password; it is gitignored but on disk, and .\** would otherwise pack it.
            Generated projects get theirs from .template.config\local-settings\, whose path does not
            end in src\Server.UI\, so this pattern cannot exclude it too. build/pack.csproj asserts
            both halves on the produced package.

            Editor and agent state never ships (Pass 56): .claude\ (Claude Code - its
            scheduled_tasks.lock appears and disappears while a session runs, and 1.2.0 shipped the
            folder itself as content/.claude/_._, so every generated project got an empty .claude),
            .vscode\, .idea\, .cursor\, and OS litter (.DS_Store, Thumbs.db, *.swp). None of it is
            tracked; it is on disk in a maintainer's working tree, which is what the nuspec packs.

            EACH FOLDER IS LISTED TWICE, and both are needed: **\.claude\** excludes the files inside,
            and **\.claude excludes the folder itself. With only the first, an EMPTY .claude folder -
            its usual state between sessions - is still packed, as the _._ placeholder NuGet writes
            for an empty directory. That is exactly how 1.2.0 shipped it; Pass 56's first pack did the
            same until the assertion in build/pack.csproj refused it.
        -->
        <file src=".\**" target="content"
              exclude="**\*.exe;**\*.nuspec;**\*.nupkg;**\bin\**;**\obj\**;**\.vs\**;**\.git\**;**\.github\**;**\wwwroot\dist\**;**\docs\**;**\doc\**;**\launchSettings.json;**\*.user;**\*.filelist;**\*.db;**\*.db-shm;**\*.db-wal;**\src\Server.UI\Files\**;**\src\Server.UI\log\**;**\src\Server.UI\appsettings.Development.json;**\GXTemplate-passes\**;**\build\**;**\tooling\**;**\Directory.Build.props;**\.claude\**;**\.claude;**\.vscode\**;**\.vscode;**\.idea\**;**\.idea;**\.cursor\**;**\.cursor;**\.DS_Store;**\Thumbs.db;**\*.swp"/>
    </files>

</package>
